{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo","id":1546392,"title":"Is Grimgroth a typo?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-25T09:36:33-08:00","id":1546392,"title":"Is Grimgroth a typo?","content":"I swear this has happened many times with famous Vampire famous characters. The names simply don't exist or in some cases are weird. I was now thinking about the (in)famous Tremere councillor and famous betrayer of the Magi, Grimgroth. Grimmroth would be a sensible germanic name, but Grimgroth doesn't seem to exist or at least I'm still to find any explanation to the etymologie of the name, I can't find anything about it. What's your take on this occurence? Do you think it was a typo and then they decided to keep it that way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T09:54:49-08:00","id":1546394,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure Goratrix is a real name either. These Tremere had funky names. Like Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T10:05:49-08:00","id":1546395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1546394#post1546394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure Goratrix is a real name either. These Tremere had funky names. Like Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh great to know that I'm not the only one who always had a problem with these names, I mean Goratrix at least sounds cool and Tremere as well (Hardestadt also, even though weird we kind of get used to it), but some others like Grimgroth definitely don't feel good, it's rather weird, I don't know how to explain lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T10:52:56-08:00","id":1546396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1546394#post1546394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure Goratrix is a real name either. These Tremere had funky names. Like Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always figured that Goratrix was a Gaul, like Asterix and Obelix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T11:29:21-08:00","id":1546399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1546396#post1546396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always figured that Goratrix was a Gaul, like Asterix and Obelix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, according to his story he is, Tremere met him in France after all, that's why I nver thought his name was that strange. Grimgroth on the other hand sounds terrible and I'm always tempted to change it lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T12:10:31-08:00","id":1546402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1546396#post1546396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always figured that Goratrix was a Gaul, like Asterix and Obelix.</div> </div> </div> </div>He is obviously Panoramix's twin who failed at reproducing the strength potion and got into vitae experiments instead. He tried to embrace Obelix but the magic of the potion reacted with the vitae and he became like an abomination with an extra powerful form of Potence. Asterix accepted the Embrace to be able to watch over him forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T13:33:29-08:00","id":1546403,"title":"","content":"There's also the lesser-known Tremere elder best known for biothaumaturgical experimentation on feline familiars and ghouls, Meowmix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T13:36:23-08:00","id":1546404,"title":"","content":"I think Grimgroth is meant to sound like a fantasy wizard\u2019s name rather than being truly Germanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T14:21:27-08:00","id":1546406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1546404#post1546404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Grimgroth is meant to sound like a fantasy wizard\u2019s name rather than being truly Germanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that as well, but that's the reason why I feel the need to change it to something more believable like &quot;Grimmroth&quot;. Grimnir would also sound cool as it's one of Odin's names, but really Grimgroth isn't to my liking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T15:15:52-08:00","id":1546408,"title":"","content":"I think this is just a legacy of RPG players inventing names that they think sound cool or interesting as opposed to &quot;realistic&quot; or &quot;historical&quot;. IIRC, Tremere was Mark Rein Hagen's character in Ars Magica as he was developing the game, and eventually this was carried into being actual canon in the Ars Magica &quot;Mythic Europe&quot; setting and later the World of Darkness. After all, we see lots of anachronistic names in Vampire for the simple fact people aren't aware of what names were popular or unpopular in different time periods or culture. And there are plenty of other made up names as well.<br /> <br /> I'm not familiar with the development of Ars Magica from 1987-1991, but I'm leaning towards that.<br /> <br /> So go ahead and change things so that it sounds better to your ears. The only people you need to justify it to are your own players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T15:55:18-08:00","id":1546410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1546408#post1546408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is just a legacy of RPG players inventing names that they think sound cool or interesting as opposed to &quot;realistic&quot; or &quot;historical&quot;. IIRC, Tremere was Mark Rein Hagen's character in Ars Magica as he was developing the game, and eventually this was carried into being actual canon in the Ars Magica &quot;Mythic Europe&quot; setting and later the World of Darkness. After all, we see lots of anachronistic names in Vampire for the simple fact people aren't aware of what names were popular or unpopular in different time periods or culture. And there are plenty of other made up names as well.<br /> <br /> I'm not familiar with the development of Ars Magica from 1987-1991, but I'm leaning towards that.<br /> <br /> So go ahead and change things so that it sounds better to your ears. The only people you need to justify it to are your own players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'm aware of the fact that Tremere was Mark Rein Hagen's character. I remember some of my friends used to joke that it's actually the reason why the Tremere were so OP in the WoD and were later HEAVILY nerfed when he left lol...<br /> <br /> I'd like to make it sound better to my ears, Grimgroth for some reason doesn't &quot;click&quot;, it's rather weird. And yes, in fact I don't need to justify it even to my players, I'm the Storyteller after all (I also surely know better as this is in fact part of my field), I'd also find it very strange indeed if a player would be somehow concerned about a sensible change of a character's name in a givern game lol<br /> <br /> The post is more about knowing what others think about it, because it happens very often that I come across a name that &quot;feels weird&quot;, so to speak, so I wanted to know if other people felt this way as well. Your explanation about it being somehow a legacy of players inventing names make sense hahaha...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 11-25-2024, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T22:15:02-08:00","id":1546421,"title":"","content":"But then again, <i>Blood Magic</i> was released after Mark Rein Hagen had already left. While the book highlight's and somehow &quot;buff&quot; Thaumaturgy it is also part of the trend &quot;that everybody and their grandma&quot; knew Thaumaturgy. Interesting fact now that I think about it, also <i>House of Tremere</i> was published after Mark left, so I'm not sure if this arguments stands, it's still funny to think about, nonetheless. A friend of mine also use to remark that it's &quot;an interesting coincidence&quot; (he would say with irony) that the whole &quot;Saulot wanted to be diablerized&quot; started after Mark left, well as I said it may mean nothing, but these things are food for thought anyway hahaha...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-29T00:43:07-08:00","id":1546481,"title":"","content":"He is a hermetic mage, with all the hermetic naming conventions it carries. Perhaps it's part of his shadow name, that would explain a lot ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7454-darthpalpy","name":"Darthpalpy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7454_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-29T18:16:35-08:00","id":1546494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darthpalpy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1546481#post1546481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He is a hermetic mage, with all the hermetic naming conventions it carries. Perhaps it's part of his shadow name, that would explain a lot ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Good theory hahaha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-02T17:39:45-08:00","id":1546548,"title":"","content":"Personally I always tried to use real or very ancient Greek, Latin, Celtic or Norse names for my player characters. Or variations of them when I tried StarFinder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-02T19:48:59-08:00","id":1546553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1546548#post1546548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I always tried to use real or very ancient Greek, Latin, Celtic or Norse names for my player characters. Or variations of them when I tried StarFinder.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, that's nice indeed. Tbh I always try to have good names for important characters in my stories, when a name sounds &quot;kind of goofy&quot; like Grimgroth, I feel like the players lose a bit of respect lol...names are very powerful things when thinking about characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-02T19:58:40-08:00","id":1546555,"title":"","content":"I just have a preference for real names and when I played elves or the odd Godling or Dragon from other games I would use ancient names. My best investment was buying a book of names when I started playing RPG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-03T20:19:41-08:00","id":1546571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1546555#post1546555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just have a preference for real names and when I played elves or the odd Godling or Dragon from other games I would use ancient names. My best investment was buying a book of names when I started playing RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, my problem is not that I feel something like &quot;a need for real names&quot;, but I need names that have some meaning. We can create new names without much effort, by combining elements of different names, researching etimology, usw. The problem is just when the names end up being &quot; kinda goofy&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-03T20:32:10-08:00","id":1546572,"title":"","content":"My book of names has all the various spellings and what it means. It's a good investment in gameplay and some of the older names are quite impressive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T15:07:49-08:00","id":1546604,"title":"","content":"The Academy of St. Gabriel (<a href=\"https://www.s-gabriel.org/names/index.shtml\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.s-gabriel.org/names/index.shtml</a>) is a repository of data regarding historical names used by the Society for Creative Anachronism. Since they require that a name be documented at some point in history, this was a group of Name Heralds who compiled historical information on naming conventions in the period covered by the SCA (5-16th Centuries). It can be a fantastic resource for finding names for elders and methuselahs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T16:41:56-08:00","id":1546608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>higgipedia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1546604#post1546604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Academy of St. Gabriel (<a href=\"https://www.s-gabriel.org/names/index.shtml\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.s-gabriel.org/names/index.shtml</a>) is a repository of data regarding historical names used by the Society for Creative Anachronism. Since they require that a name be documented at some point in history, this was a group of Name Heralds who compiled historical information on naming conventions in the period covered by the SCA (5-16th Centuries). It can be a fantastic resource for finding names for elders and methuselahs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much! Now I have another nice resource to rely on! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T17:00:38-08:00","id":1546610,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the additional information higgipedia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-12T20:19:51-08:00","id":1546913,"title":"","content":"Those are their <b><i>Magi </i></b>names, adopted upon being acepted as full-fledged members of the House of Tremere of the Order of Hermes, like it was pretty much the norm for any character following the setting conventions of Ars Magica?<br /> <br /> Kind of came naturally with the terrain to me, but maybe that's because i'm an old fart from before most of these links being shaved off and shoehorned in some version or other of Mage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Grimgroth was a little nod to a forgotten, forsaken even, past, that somehow keeps on persisting and even being reused, all notion of incongruity involved utterly missed.<br /> <br /> Goratrix might not be &quot;a straight from the other game&quot; port like Grim, but was definitely made with the &quot;mix historical with some fantasy fancy/nonsense&quot; naming conventions of the Auld Game in mind. Much like Meerlinda, Etrius &amp; Abetorius, for that matter.<br /> For me this always served also as a stealth hint of the age tiers of each councillor, separating the once mages turned vampires from those actually embraced into a full-fledged Tremere vampire clan, where such &quot;shadow name&quot; trappings were little more than relics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-12-2024, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T06:24:02-08:00","id":1546963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1546913#post1546913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are their <b><i>Magi </i></b>names, adopted upon being acepted as full-fledged members of the House of Tremere of the Order of Hermes, like it was pretty much the norm for any character following the setting conventions of Ars Magica?<br /> <br /> Kind of came naturally with the terrain to me, but maybe that's because i'm an old fart from before most of these links being shaved off and shoehorned in some version or other of Mage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Grimgroth was a little nod to a forgotten, forsaken even, past, that somehow keeps on persisting and even being reused, all notion of incongruity involved utterly missed.<br /> <br /> Goratrix might not be &quot;a straight from the other game&quot; port like Grim, but was definitely made with the &quot;mix historical with some fantasy fancy/nonsense&quot; naming conventions of the Auld Game in mind. Much like Meerlinda, Etrius &amp; Abetorius, for that matter.<br /> For me this always served also as a stealth hint of the age tiers of each councillor, separating the once mages turned vampires from those actually embraced into a full-fledged Tremere vampire clan, where such &quot;shadow name&quot; trappings were little more than relics.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point you make. It's intresting that later the setting decide to change things a little in this regard, or at least that's the impression I got with characters like Lothar (Lotharius) that Dark Ages Vampire brought into the fold as he was one of the first outside the Concil of Seven to be embraced into the clan (and if half the stories about him are true, he's a very impressive individual).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T11:25:04-08:00","id":1546971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1546963#post1546963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a good point you make. It's intresting that later the setting decide to change things a little in this regard, or at least that's the impression I got with characters like Lothar (Lotharius) that Dark Ages Vampire brought into the fold as he was one of the first outside the Concil of Seven to be embraced into the clan (and if half the stories about him are true, he's a very impressive individual).</div> </div> </div> </div>Lotharius is an interesting case indeed, since he first appears in late '93 on Berlin by Night, as the name of Justicar Karl Schrekt's sire. Later on he would get fleshed out by Feder &amp; Schwert's Wiener Blut: Wien bei Nacht in '97, that would serve as main inspiration to the version of Dark Ages: Europe and later books.<br /> <br /> (Also, Lotharius <i>did </i>happen to be a common latinization of Lothar and its variants back in the middle ages, so in the end all of that leaves the matter of his past pre-embrace provenance very much in the air)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T12:52:14-08:00","id":1546977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1546971#post1546971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lotharius is an interesting case indeed, since he first appears in late '93 on Berlin by Night, as the name of Justicar Karl Schrekt's sire. Later on he would get fleshed out by Feder &amp; Schwert's Wiener Blut: Wien bei Nacht in '97, that would serve as main inspiration to the version of Dark Ages: Europe and later books.<br /> <br /> (Also, Lotharius <i>did </i>happen to be a common latinization of Lothar and its variants back in the middle ages, so in the end all of that leaves the matter of his past pre-embrace provenance very much in the air)</div> </div> </div> </div>Lotharius was born in Cologne, if I'm not mistaken, it's one of the few things about him that his text is &quot;somewhat clear&quot; about.<br /> I prefer to call him Lothar, because it sounds much cooler than Lotharius lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T12:53:59-08:00","id":1546978,"title":"","content":"Lotharius and Lothar are both cool sounding names to me and would make cool shadow names for a Mage The Awakening game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T12:59:55-08:00","id":1546981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1546978#post1546978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lotharius and Lothar are both cool sounding names to me and would make cool shadow names for a Mage The Awakening game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, tbh I like the name, it's just that when you speak a lot of Spanish and Portuguese &quot;Lotharius&quot; sounds a bit different to the ear, but it's ok. The fact that his text mention that he was once an Oracle is quite intriguing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T13:02:02-08:00","id":1546983,"title":"","content":"I know what you mean when it comes to hearing Lotharius and you think of a playboy type of character as such people were called Lothario's and I just showed how old I am by remembering that statement.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T13:09:36-08:00","id":1546987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1546394#post1546394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure Goratrix is a real name either. These Tremere had funky names. Like Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they were shadow names that they used to conceal there true names like they do in the Mage The Awakening setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-14T13:57:01-08:00","id":1546996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1546983#post1546983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know what you mean when it comes to hearing Lotharius and you think of a playboy type of character as such people were called Lothario's and I just showed how old I am by remembering that statement.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So you get exactly what I mean hahaha...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-02T04:03:58-08:00","id":1547451,"title":"","content":"Also Lothar is the name of one of the main villains of the Voltron series. I'm a fan of transforming robots and as a kid I was drawn to such things and the name stuck out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-07T10:56:27-07:00","id":1559274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1546555#post1546555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just have a preference for real names and when I played elves or the odd Godling or Dragon from other games I would use ancient names. My best investment was buying a book of names when I started playing RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>For elves, I simply get some old germanic with &quot;-ulf&quot; for prefix, replace with &quot;-alf&quot; and job done.<br /> Certainly worked for a certain grey wizard of Tolkien. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-07-2026, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-07T11:39:25-07:00","id":1559278,"title":"","content":"I use mostly Greek, Latin, Spanish and Irish names for my elves and dragons and the occasional Persian name if it really sounds great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-11T08:19:26-07:00","id":1559351,"title":"","content":"Since we're slowly necroing this thread, I'll chime in. The problem with &quot;Grimgroth&quot; is the weird mix of consonants that aren't that natural in English. &quot;Grimgoth&quot; would sound more natural. &quot;Grimroth&quot; also works. Even &quot;Grimgroff&quot; would be slightly better, though I think people would instinctively want to pronounce it &quot;Grimgoth&quot; anyway.<br /> <br /> I tend to use name generators a lot these days, but each one can only be used a few times before it starts getting repetitive. I like looking at names from mythology or searching for names with thematic resonance.<br /> <br /> For example, for an STV title I'm working on, covering the Tremere <i>antitribu</i>, I wanted to reintroduce an epic Dark Ages character as the new leader of House Goratrix. I eventually settled on &quot;Abdelygma&quot;, adapted from the Greek &quot;bdelygma&quot;, a descriptor for the Whore of Babylon, meaning &quot;abomination&quot;. I really wanted to use &quot;Kostroma&quot;, a fertility goddess whose name means &quot;bonfire&quot; (especially poignant given the <i>antitribu'</i>s near-demise), but it's East Slavic and the character I had in mind is Romanian. But Biblical stuff works because the Romanians were Christian at that time, and elder Tremere would know classical languages anyway.<br /> <br /> Another Spellbinder character is called S\u00e9bastien P\u00e9ch\u00e9, taken from his modelling days. He was an HIV+ artist's muse, posing for mythic and religious-themed portraits in the style of Pierre et Gilles. St. Sebastian was a common subject of Pierre et Gilles, and is often seen as a patron saint of gay men; &quot;P\u00e9ch\u00e9&quot; means &quot;Sin&quot;. So he's &quot;Sebastian of Sin&quot;, a kind of patron saint of queer martyrdom. He's now a Knight Inquisitor, so I've stuck him in Montreal, where he's dreaming about Metathiax (the disease demon) and has committed to destroying it. The name and the story fed into each other nicely and helped me really flesh him out.<br /> <br /> For the Telyavs, I'm looking into Lithuanian gods to give me some ideas. I'm having a lot of fun. Then I'll have to do Mexican names for the main chantry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 04-11-2026, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-11T15:13:44-07:00","id":1559361,"title":"","content":"<i>House of Tremere </i>explains all of this indirectly. On PG 87 Malgorzata's background explains &quot;She combined her own name, her masters', and that of a local goddess of evil magic to give herself the mage name of Malgorzata.&quot; Basically when Magi entered the art formally they renamed themselves to whatever they felt sounded cool. It didn't/doesn't matter if it is strictly correct to whatever convention a language/society would use. Vibe based naming~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-12T02:37:01-07:00","id":1559369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1559361#post1559361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>House of Tremere </i>explains all of this indirectly. On PG 87 Malgorzata's background explains &quot;She combined her own name, her masters', and that of a local goddess of evil magic to give herself the mage name of Malgorzata.&quot; Basically when Magi entered the art formally they renamed themselves to whatever they felt sounded cool. It didn't/doesn't matter if it is strictly correct to whatever convention a language/society would use. Vibe based naming~</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. It's definitely vibes-based. Though I think that's partly a convenience for OOC reasons (WW writers having fewer readily available tools for research back then). If you take Malgorzata, for example, her name is actually just the Polish version of Margaret. And while &quot;Mal-&quot; could come from her mortal name (Malana) and &quot;-gor-&quot; from Goratrix, I couldn't find an Eastern European goddess of dark magic whose name includes &quot;-zata&quot;. Perhaps they meant Marzanna or perhaps Midnight Zorya, which would have made her Malgorzanna or Malgorzorya/Malgorya instead. My best guess is they came up with the name first, though, and then made up an etymology afterwards.<br /> <br /> So you do have a lot of latitude. But I reason that anyone who was Embraced as one of the early Tremere would also be a huge geek, so if you can sneak extra layers of meaning into their name, it's even better. Or maybe that's just me, since I get overly excited by cool etymologies! \ud83d\ude02<br /> <br /> Someone with more technical skill could probably program a name generator that mixes 2\u20134 syllables together in a vaguely convincing way to come up with these shadow names\u2014there's already something like this for Exalted. In the meantime, I've had some decent results with this generator: <a href=\"https://www.scabard.com/world-building/character/class/magician/random/name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.scabard.com/world-buildi...name-generator</a>.<br /> <br /> I use the following prompt: &quot;Mononymous, House Tremere-style names for Vampire: The Masquerade, mixing two to four syllables from mythically and mystically important names and words, rooted in classical and ancient languages (Latin, Greek, Aramaic, Hebrew, Celtic, etc), with gravitas. Avoid cutesy or on-the-nose names.&quot;<br /> <br /> That gives some names that sound suitably epic enough. You may want to swap syllables around between the suggested words, or play around with swapping vowels and consonants, but it's good for inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-16T18:09:44-07:00","id":1559472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, for an STV title I'm working on, covering the Tremere <i>antitribu</i>, I wanted to reintroduce an epic Dark Ages character as the new leader of House Goratrix. I eventually settled on &quot;Abdelygma&quot;, adapted from the Greek &quot;bdelygma&quot;, a descriptor for the Whore of Babylon, meaning &quot;abomination&quot;. </div> </div> </div>My meme-infested brain accidentally parsed it as &quot;Abdel Lygma&quot;, to my deepest regret and pain of things i can't unthink.<br /> <br /> <br /> (But as an aside, i have tinkered with the idea of Goratrix being pseudo-celtic and him a rogue member of the Di\u00e9dne, the Order of Hermes &quot;druidic house&quot; who changed houses and would be eventually responsible for its fall in one of the many steps of the road to the foundation of the Tremere as kindred bloodline and then clan)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-17T12:51:02-07:00","id":1559487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1546421#post1546421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then again, <i>Blood Magic</i> was released after Mark Rein Hagen had already left. While the book highlight's and somehow &quot;buff&quot; Thaumaturgy it is also part of the trend &quot;that everybody and their grandma&quot; knew Thaumaturgy. Interesting fact now that I think about it, also <i>House of Tremere</i> was published after Mark left, so I'm not sure if this arguments stands, it's still funny to think about, nonetheless. A friend of mine also use to remark that it's &quot;an interesting coincidence&quot; (he would say with irony) that the whole &quot;Saulot wanted to be diablerized&quot; started after Mark left, well as I said it may mean nothing, but these things are food for thought anyway hahaha...</div> </div> </div> </div>Late to the party but here I go...<br /> <br /> both things can be true at once. Tremere were overpowered as one of the main things that sold supplements was new powers and Tremere was both the easiest to create new powers and those powers were easily obtainable even by lower level Cainites. And so we ended up with myriad of &quot;Do What You Want&quot; Path. So Tremere were prime target for nerfs. <br /> <br /> Also, Thaumaturgy was a system of codified rules for Blood Magic in the hermetic vein but Blood Magic was there long before Tremere so giving it to Setites or Assamites made sense.<br /> <br /> As for the topic of names: de gustibuus... But the argument that Grimgroth does not sound like a real name does not make sense. Many vampires change their names when they become Embraced or to cut ties to their former existencelater in their unlife. But your and your players' fun is most important so feel free to change names you do not like. It's your game.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-18T13:29:12-07:00","id":1559507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1559487#post1559487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the topic of names: de gustibuus... But the argument that Grimgroth does not sound like a real name does not make sense. Many vampires change their names when they become Embraced or to cut ties to their former existencelater in their unlife. But your and your players' fun is most important so feel free to change names you do not like. It's your game.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that it's a made-up name that's the problem, I think. The name has nine letters in it and a whopping seven of them are consonants. &quot;Grim-&quot; and &quot;-groth&quot; are closed syllables, constricting and &quot;pinching&quot; the vowel sounds and emphasising the consonants at the end of each. It has a very harsh mix of phonemes that require awkward positioning in the mouth to pronounce. &quot;-Groth&quot; is also not a standard word or syllable in English, but it sounds like a mix of syllables that are more common.<br /> <br /> So, with &quot;Grim-&quot;, you start at the back of your throat for a &quot;g&quot;, roll it forward for an &quot;r&quot;, move it up for an &quot;i&quot;, and end on an &quot;m&quot;, moving the sound to the front of your mouth as you close your lips. That's fairly simple and fluid on its own, but the &quot;m&quot; feels like that's where the name should end. That's why names like &quot;Maugrim&quot; or &quot;Anngrim&quot; feel quite satisfying. You can put &quot;Grim-&quot; at the start, but the syllables that follow are usually simpler and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bouba/kiki_effect\" target=\"_blank\">rounder</a>, so the overall effect is less disjointed (&quot;Grimaldo&quot;, &quot;Grimild&quot;, &quot;Grimshaw&quot; or the very rare &quot;Grimbald&quot;).<br /> <br /> But then with &quot;-groth&quot;, you get a &quot;spiky&quot; consonant again. You have to quickly pull the sound to the back of your throat again, roll it forward again, but then drop the noise in your mouth and draw it forward for the &quot;o&quot; and slide your tongue forward for the &quot;th&quot;. The spikiness puts the &quot;m&quot; and the &quot;gr&quot; at odds. Your brain also instinctively wants to repeat the first syllable again, but then gets diverted. It's a sort of uncanny valley effect, worsened by the clunky consonants and clipped vowels.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, the result is a juddering start-stop that is particularly counterintuitive on first pronunciation. You have to practice it in your head a few times to get it right. Compared with &quot;Tremere&quot;, &quot;Goratrix&quot;, &quot;Etrius&quot; or &quot;Malgorzata&quot;, which alternate consonants and syllables in a more natural-sounding way, it's a clunky mess. &quot;Grimroth&quot; is more balanced. But even &quot;Grimgoth&quot; is easier on the ear, as you at least lose the uncanny valley thing (&quot;-goth&quot; is easier and more familiar than &quot;-groth&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-23T03:20:41-07:00","id":1559579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1559507#post1559507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not that it's a made-up name that's the problem, I think. The name has nine letters in it and a whopping seven of them are consonants. &quot;Grim-&quot; and &quot;-groth&quot; are closed syllables, constricting and &quot;pinching&quot; the vowel sounds and emphasising the consonants at the end of each. It has a very harsh mix of phonemes that require awkward positioning in the mouth to pronounce. &quot;-Groth&quot; is also not a standard word or syllable in English, but it sounds like a mix of syllables that are more common.<br /> <br /> So, with &quot;Grim-&quot;, you start at the back of your throat for a &quot;g&quot;, roll it forward for an &quot;r&quot;, move it up for an &quot;i&quot;, and end on an &quot;m&quot;, moving the sound to the front of your mouth as you close your lips. That's fairly simple and fluid on its own, but the &quot;m&quot; feels like that's where the name should end. That's why names like &quot;Maugrim&quot; or &quot;Anngrim&quot; feel quite satisfying. You can put &quot;Grim-&quot; at the start, but the syllables that follow are usually simpler and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bouba/kiki_effect\" target=\"_blank\">rounder</a>, so the overall effect is less disjointed (&quot;Grimaldo&quot;, &quot;Grimild&quot;, &quot;Grimshaw&quot; or the very rare &quot;Grimbald&quot;).<br /> <br /> But then with &quot;-groth&quot;, you get a &quot;spiky&quot; consonant again. You have to quickly pull the sound to the back of your throat again, roll it forward again, but then drop the noise in your mouth and draw it forward for the &quot;o&quot; and slide your tongue forward for the &quot;th&quot;. The spikiness puts the &quot;m&quot; and the &quot;gr&quot; at odds. Your brain also instinctively wants to repeat the first syllable again, but then gets diverted. It's a sort of uncanny valley effect, worsened by the clunky consonants and clipped vowels.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, the result is a juddering start-stop that is particularly counterintuitive on first pronunciation. You have to practice it in your head a few times to get it right. Compared with &quot;Tremere&quot;, &quot;Goratrix&quot;, &quot;Etrius&quot; or &quot;Malgorzata&quot;, which alternate consonants and syllables in a more natural-sounding way, it's a clunky mess. &quot;Grimroth&quot; is more balanced. But even &quot;Grimgoth&quot; is easier on the ear, as you at least lose the uncanny valley thing (&quot;-goth&quot; is easier and more familiar than &quot;-groth&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>You explained it perfectly. The real problem here is not only that it's a &quot;made-up name&quot;, but rather that it doesn't sound good. As you explained, it's rather &quot;convoluted&quot; to pronounce and as such I find it much preferably to &quot;fix it&quot; by changing it. I have players that speak only Portuguese and Grimgroth would be a nightmare for them to pronounce well and that's one of the factors I take into consideration when I use an NPC that's supposed to be so impactful as one would expect a Councillor to be. I don't want them to pronounce it wrong as names carry a lot of weight in a character's construction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-25T18:24:10-07:00","id":1559628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1559579#post1559579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You explained it perfectly. The real problem here is not only that it's a &quot;made-up name&quot;, but rather that it doesn't sound good. As you explained, it's rather &quot;convoluted&quot; to pronounce and as such I find it much preferably to &quot;fix it&quot; by changing it. I have players that speak only Portuguese and Grimgroth would be a nightmare for them to pronounce well and that's one of the factors I take into consideration when I use an NPC that's supposed to be so impactful as one would expect a Councillor to be. I don't want them to pronounce it wrong as names carry a lot of weight in a character's construction.</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re right. Grimgroth does sound a little awkward. Etrius is a much easier sounding name for a Tremere elder.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-05T08:50:08-07:00","id":1559789,"title":"","content":"In all fairness vampire society being full of characters who would give linguists conniptions if any professional linguist ever found out about them because they came up with a name they thought was <i>so cool</i> umpteen generations ago and have refused to be told that the name makes <i>no damn sense</i> linguistically ever since seems to be quite on-brand.<br /> <br /> (Especially if you like a little bit of WHAT WE DO IN THE SHADOWS unselfconsciousness in your elder vampires: just be careful to pick nits around the \u201cI might even care about your opinion if you live to be older than at least three cities on non-adjacent continents\u201d elder and not the \u201cI do not care about your opinion, but could tell you were mocking me\u201d type of Elder*).<br /> <br /> <br /> *Where the shift to past tense indicates that somebody is now just plain dead, no \u2018un-\u2018 required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-05T11:34:11-07:00","id":1559791,"title":"","content":"I really like using real old world names for many of my supernatural beings as promotes a sense of authority or otherworldly vibes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-06T02:58:42-07:00","id":1559802,"title":"","content":"So do I, but there\u2019s no reason actual Old World names can\u2019t be mixed in with names only a very, very specific sort of vampire could possibly think of as cool - not to mention names so blatantly innocuous that they\u2019re obviously cover identities - because variety is the spice of life (and possibly even un-death) you know.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T07:13:10-07:00","id":1561822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1559361#post1559361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>House of Tremere </i>explains all of this indirectly. On PG 87 Malgorzata's background explains &quot;She combined her own name, her masters', and that of a local goddess of evil magic to give herself the mage name of Malgorzata.&quot; Basically when Magi entered the art formally they renamed themselves to whatever they felt sounded cool. It didn't/doesn't matter if it is strictly correct to whatever convention a language/society would use. Vibe based naming~</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to see someone call Grimgroth out on his name:<br /> <br /> &quot;I am Grimgroth of the Tremere Council of Seven. You...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Grimgroth? What kind of name is that?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's my shadow name! It's the name of power that I chose for myself when I became a magi...&quot;<br /> &quot;But it makes no sense!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What do you mean, it makes no sense?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, it's not Latin. It sounds vaguely Germanic, but it's not. It's got way too many consonants; maybe Grimgoth might have worked better.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I rather liked the vibe of Grimgroth. It's grim, and it's...grothy?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But it doesn't mean anything! It's just a random assortment of letters!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That's it!&quot; Grimgroth frenzies.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28946-pryderi","name":"Pryderi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T09:36:34-07:00","id":1561825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pryderi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1561822#post1561822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd love to see someone call Grimgroth out on his name:<br /> <br /> &quot;I am Grimgroth of the Tremere Council of Seven. You...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Grimgroth? What kind of name is that?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's my shadow name! It's the name of power that I chose for myself when I became a magi...&quot;<br /> &quot;But it makes no sense!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What do you mean, it makes no sense?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, it's not Latin. It sounds vaguely Germanic, but it's not. It's got way too many consonants; maybe Grimgoth might have worked better.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I rather liked the vibe of Grimgroth. It's grim, and it's...grothy?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But it doesn't mean anything! It's just a random assortment of letters!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That's it!&quot; Grimgroth frenzies.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, the DA: Mage Grimoire actually just spells it Grimgoth. Like Daimonion (versus Daimoinon), it makes way more sense and is much easier on the ear than the original.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T11:10:45-07:00","id":1561830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pryderi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1561822#post1561822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd love to see someone call Grimgroth out on his name:<br /> <br /> &quot;I am Grimgroth of the Tremere Council of Seven. You...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Grimgroth? What kind of name is that?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's my shadow name! It's the name of power that I chose for myself when I became a magi...&quot;<br /> &quot;But it makes no sense!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What do you mean, it makes no sense?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, it's not Latin. It sounds vaguely Germanic, but it's not. It's got way too many consonants; maybe Grimgoth might have worked better.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I rather liked the vibe of Grimgroth. It's grim, and it's...grothy?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But it doesn't mean anything! It's just a random assortment of letters!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That's it!&quot; Grimgroth frenzies.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's way more common in history than you imagine, and worse things too.<br /> <br /> A weird amount of historical figures are actually known by names they chose at 15yo, and you can be sure that when the actual full name is translated, it shows.<br /> <br /> Let's just say that if modern English were used in the Middle Ages or Antiquity, you could have a general called Destrotter. From &quot;Death Stroke The Terminator&quot;. Also a lot of variations using Batman and Spiderman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T11:39:07-07:00","id":1561833,"title":"","content":"Lots of people forget that language evolves over time as words change or fall out of use. Just think how many historical figures are better known for nicknames or titles rather than then their actual name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T12:20:29-07:00","id":1561836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546392-is-grimgroth-a-typo?p=1561833#post1561833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of people forget that language evolves over time as words change or fall out of use. Just think how many historical figures are better known for nicknames or titles rather than then their actual name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your idea of &quot;actual name&quot; doesn't even work in most societies, it's incredibly recent for something so widespread today.<br /> <br /> In Rome there was no &quot;actual name&quot; until adulthood. Your &quot;name&quot; was a number at best. At adulthood you'd be a participant in the process of making your definitive name.<br /> <br /> Japan until recently gave people several names through life, and they were all actual names. Baby names were simple and easy, so you don't get to attached before some assurance the child will likely live. At 6, then 11 IIRC, you had special coming of age ceremonies with a new name. You'd make your own <i>first</i> adult name at 15 with almost no rules, and 8 years later would be granted the opportunity to regret your past decision and try again. Titles and official roles were also partly conveyed through name, so promotions in the hierarchy usually led to new naming ceremonies were you could change whatever you wanted.<br /> <br /> For Germanic peoples your &quot;actual name&quot; is a personal one-word name and the family name of your father, but for Iberians (including LatAm) it's a personal 1-3 words name (because the traditional pool is smaller and some names are hugely popular), then 1-2 surnames from your mother's family, then 1-2 surnames from your father's family. I have 4 names and I'm not unusual in the Iberian world.<br /> <br /> So people in some times and places could have <b><u><i>actual names</i></u></b> we'd consider childish and stupid. And &quot;variations of Batman&quot; are basically the most common rule in history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T14:17:58-07:00","id":1561845,"title":"","content":"My Zimbabwean aunt (&quot;adoptive&quot; aunt but it's more complicated than that) has seven names. I used to be incredibly proud I could remember them all. She chose the name Wendy (from <i>Peter Pan</i>) when she came over to the UK, but as her first name was Tanyaradzwa anyway, my mum just called her Tanya. Her &quot;English&quot; name never even got used, but it still sits there.<br /> <br /> I think she doesn't have her maiden name on official legal documents either, but I always add it in when doing the whole shebang. In for a penny and all that, right? \ud83d\ude02","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}